# Conventional Commits

Every commit message in this repository **must** follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/).

## Format

```text
<type>(<optional-scope>): <short description>

[optional body]

[optional footer]
```

- Subject in **English**, imperative mood, no trailing period
- Keep the first line ≤ 72 characters
- `type` is required; `scope` is optional

## Allowed types

| Type | Use when |
|---|---|
| `feat` | New user-facing capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Formatting; no logic change |
| `refactor` | Code change that is not a feat or fix |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `test` | Add or fix tests |
| `build` | Dependencies, packaging, Docker |
| `ci` | GitHub Actions / CI config |
| `chore` | Maintenance that does not fit above |

## Examples

```text
feat(estimations): require 100-char minimum transcription
fix(llm): handle empty Anthropic text blocks
docs(readme): document Docker make targets
ci: run smoke tests inside the Docker image
chore(rules): add conventional commits cursor rule
```

## Do not

```text
# ❌ BAD
Updated stuff
fix: fixed bug.
FEAT: Add endpoint
wip
```

When creating commits for the user, always draft the message in this format.

## Related gates

- Pre-commit also enforces **coverage ≥ 90%** (`coverage-90.mdc`) before the commit is created.
- Commit-msg hook validates Conventional Commits via `.pre-commit-config.yaml`.
